                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4c512b2f-97ed-3fc1-aa37-93b128649e42",
                        "entry_id": "285ce87a-7a6e-3643-9987-0adeb3f9069c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of a voice: characterized by clarity, fullness, smoothness, and strength of sound; hence, of a person: having a clear, full, and strong voice, appropriate for public speaking, reading aloud, etc."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52a2d93f-104a-3fa0-8764-f7b420a63a38",
                        "entry_id": "285ce87a-7a6e-3643-9987-0adeb3f9069c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of writing, etc.: clear, effective, powerful."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "518c4c66-987c-3ac4-b343-d5a6374d0537",
                        "entry_id": "285ce87a-7a6e-3643-9987-0adeb3f9069c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of speech or writing: bombastic, pompous."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly",
                            "derogatory"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "43fa34b1-b027-4370-baa0-bb538fe76560",
                                "sense_id": "518c4c66-987c-3ac4-b343-d5a6374d0537",
                                "text": "A series of U.N. and government officials spoke. […] In orotund turns of phrase—indeed, in spiraling helices of phrase; in snarled fishing lines of phrase; in endless small intestines of phrase--the speakers ingeniously explored and invented connections between qwerty, alphabetical filing, and socioeconomic advance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2616178-06ce-44d8-b5cd-c05069a01ede",
                                "sense_id": "518c4c66-987c-3ac4-b343-d5a6374d0537",
                                "text": "He would also, you can't help thinking, have approved [Alan] Hollinghurst's discriminating eye and perhaps even enjoyed the half-facetious, half-adoring tributes Nick pays to his famously orotund late style, the \"plums of periphrasis\" Nick likes to slip into his conversation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5e37484-3ff4-473d-b0f5-cff4f69c5727",
                                "sense_id": "518c4c66-987c-3ac4-b343-d5a6374d0537",
                                "text": "When Groucho Marx was once asked a long and orotund question, he replied, \"Whom knows?\" […] The popularity of \"whom\" humour tells us two things about the distinction between \"who\" and \"whom\". First, \"whom\" has long been perceived as formal verging on pompous. Second, the rules for its proper use are obscure to many speakers, tempting them to drop \"whom\" into their speech whenever they want to sound posh."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "525a2ef5-04d8-4f1c-ae49-1940f740e94d",
                        "source_entry_id": "285ce87a-7a6e-3643-9987-0adeb3f9069c",
                        "source_sense_description": "of a voice: characterized by clarity, fullness, smoothness, and strength of sound",
                        "target_lang_word": "sonor",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sonor",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb251599-a31d-308e-b960-fa9e1378ccb9",
                                        "entry_id": "3202c06b-703a-33c7-a4b6-59ec932b7304",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "klangvoll"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139f6151-f353-4896-ac2b-693f8b95c206",
                                                "sense_id": "eb251599-a31d-308e-b960-fa9e1378ccb9",
                                                "text": "Er hat eine sonore Stimme."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfdfec65-f157-309d-bbac-d18f905009ad",
                                        "entry_id": "3202c06b-703a-33c7-a4b6-59ec932b7304",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Linguistik, speziell Eigenschaft der Lautklassen, die im Verhältnis zu anderen eine höhere Schallfülle aufweisen und deshalb besser wahrnehmbar sind"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Phonetik"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2192a3a3-51db-4f03-8b25-f1105b3e4b5b",
                                                "sense_id": "bfdfec65-f157-309d-bbac-d18f905009ad",
                                                "text": "„Der Silbengipfel ist also das sonorste Segment in der Silbe.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ebdc404-cb12-4063-a961-4ae354a9d36e",
                                                "sense_id": "bfdfec65-f157-309d-bbac-d18f905009ad",
                                                "text": "„Problematisch sind als einsilbig angesehene, aber der Sonorität nach zweigipflige Wörter…, denn Sibilanten sind sonorer als Klusile.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c2ee971-78a2-3049-9111-e9406eaf8a35",
                                        "entry_id": "3202c06b-703a-33c7-a4b6-59ec932b7304",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "klangvoll, volltönend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48cbc7a8-7d97-475b-8013-0e756f263cd7",
                                                "sense_id": "3c2ee971-78a2-3049-9111-e9406eaf8a35",
                                                "text": "Man kann einen sonoren Klopfschall vernehmen."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
